Third-party content
-------------------

The following content in this pack comes from third parties under their own
terms.

Data (system-solar/data/)

Orbits, physical properties and rotation of the bodies are facts, taken from:

- NASA/JPL Horizons (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/) and the JPL planetary
  satellite mean elements (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/sats/elem/),
  NASA/JPL-Caltech Solar System Dynamics Group. US government work, public
  domain. Orbits are fitted to Horizons positions.
- The IAU WGCCRE report on cartographic coordinates and rotational elements
  (Archinal et al. 2018, Celestial Mechanics and Dynamical Astronomy 130:22).
- Sol by RSS-Reborn (https://github.com/RSS-Reborn), for a few values neither
  source provides.

Material base colors (system-solar/resources/materials/)

For bodies whose maps these scripts do not generate: the average color of the
body's map in Sol by RSS-Reborn (https://github.com/RSS-Reborn), measured by
scripts/sol_base_colors.py.

Skybox (system-solar/resources/textures/skyboxes/)

Deep Star Maps 2020, NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center Scientific Visualization
Studio (https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4851). Gaia DR2: ESA/Gaia/DPAC. Hipparcos-2,
Tycho-2: ESA. Used under the NASA media usage guidelines; the cube map is
converted from the source EXR.

Moon textures (system-solar/resources/textures/bodies/luna/)

CGI Moon Kit, NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio
(https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4720): color from the Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter
Camera Hapke-normalized Wide Angle Camera mosaic, polar latitudes from the Lunar
Orbiter Laser Altimeter albedo map; elevation from the Lunar Orbiter Laser
Altimeter gridded data. Used under the NASA media usage guidelines; resampled,
and the normal map derived from the elevation.
